ApplySkillWithConditionalRandom - Applies skill effect with conditional random value generation

Algorithm:
1. Validate input parameters (pSkillObject cannot be NULL)
2. If pOwnerUnit is valid and type==4 (skill unit), apply passive synergies first
3. Load min/max values from pSkillData structure (offsets +0x8, +0xc)
4. Compare min vs max values to determine if randomization is needed
5. If min==max, use fixed value; otherwise generate random value in range [min,max]
6. Select appropriate RNG seed based on pSkillObject validity and structure
7. Call ApplySkillWithShiftedValue with generated/fixed value
8. Return boolean result indicating success/failure of skill application

Parameters:
@param nUnused - Unused parameter (legacy/reserved)
@param pOwnerUnit - Pointer to unit that owns/triggers the skill (UnitAny*)
@param pSkillObject - Pointer to skill object structure (SkillStruct*)
@param pSkillData - Pointer to skill data/configuration structure (SkillData*)
@param nShiftValue - Value used for skill effect shifting/scaling calculations
@param wStatId - 16-bit stat identifier for passive synergy lookup
@param pParam7 - Additional parameter (purpose unknown, void*)
@param pParam8 - Additional parameter (purpose unknown, void*) 
@param pRelatedData1 - Related skill/unit data pointer (void*)
@param pRelatedData2 - Related skill/unit data pointer (void*)

Returns:
@return bool - true if skill effect was successfully applied, false on failure

NOTES: Function uses conditional randomization - if min==max in skill data,
applies fixed value; otherwise generates random value in [min,max] range
